WEBVTT

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:11.990
F. Nightingale

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.900
What are you talking about?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.400
You mean the group names were hints...

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.120
or actually the solutions somehow?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.250
We just explained it.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.630
Now, now.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.600
The order of the group's planet from the sun

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.940
and the names of the
students in each group...

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.790
That was the key to figuring out the VIP.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.210
Does that much make sense?

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.460
Mars is the fourth planet from the sun.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.680
If we sort the Mars group students
into Japanese alphabetical order,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.900
it goes: Ayanokoji-kun, Ichinose-san,
Ibuki-san, Karuizawa-san.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.630
That's why I'm the VIP?

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:56.780
And the third name in the Earth group,
Kushida-san, was the VIP.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.430
But isn't that system a little...

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.490
Simple.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:02.540
Yeah, that!

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.810
Once you know the rule, it's simple.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.500
But figuring it out during
the test wouldn't be.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.640
There'd be no way to confirm the rule
just from knowing your own class's VIPs.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.800
Indeed.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.550
But not for Ryuen-kun.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:20.290
He apparently figured out the rule early on.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.030
But he made a mistake.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.060
Perhaps he forgot that
Class C is not a monolith.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.930
Class C isn't fully under
Ryuen-kun's control, you mean?

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.560
A dictatorship frequently fosters a
populace unhappy with its oppressor.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:39.200
The error could have come from
a student not under his control.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.940
I wonder about that.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.340
Perhaps maintaining leadership
is a difficult thing.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.060
Maybe so.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:52.420
Still, I'm glad you came to
us with this, Horikita-san.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.080
What choice did I have?

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.970
There may be tests coming up
that I can't pass on my own.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.010
Very probable!

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.040
As long as that's the case,

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.470
it'll be important to have
some quantity of connections.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.480
<i>Yes.</i>

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.630
<i>There are limits to how
hard one can fight alone.</i>

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.980
2nd Season

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.980
Classroom
of
the
Elite

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.280
The second term starts today.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.000
From the month of September
through early October,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.030
we'll have more gym classes than usual,

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.500
in preparation for the
upcoming sports festival.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:58.750
I've given you your new schedules and
the sports festival documentation.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.560
You can find the same information
on the school home page.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.260
Regarding Sports Festival and Competition Points
Point Distributions

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.810
Compare them if you must.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:06.860
Ma'am!

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.270
Is the sports festival
one of our special tests?

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.890
You can interpret it that way if you wish.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:18.750
Though whatever you call it, it will
have a major influence on your class.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.900
Cruelty unchained!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:22.850
Heck yeah!

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:24.500
Time for me to shine!

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:24.500
Sports festival...

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.910
For this year's sports festival,

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.890
the entire school will compete
as Team Red and Team White.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.670
You of Class D along with
Class A will be Team Red.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.670
We're teamed up with Class A?

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.750
Along with second- and third-years...

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.420
Seems annoying.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.430
I'm gonna carry Team Red to the win!

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.730
Let's raise hands to speak, everyone.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:51.060
Keep it down, guys!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.930
Are you thinking about how you'll
finally get a chance to see him?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.570
Don't talk about that here.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.650
I won't tell you a second time.

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:13.930
Right.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:18.000
First, read through your materials.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:22.500
Events consist of mandatory
and voluntary events.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:29.480
<i>Generally speaking, voluntary events
grant more points than mandatory ones.</i>

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.890
It's important to give all
you have to every event.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.390
The student who places last in individual events loses 1,000 PPt.
(If private points are currently below 1,000, penalty will be applied to written exams)

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.770
The penalty for losing is severe.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.630
Ma'am.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.270
What's this about bonuses
for the top three placers?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.670
What's this about adding
points to written exams?

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.460
It's exactly what it sounds like.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.010
By placing in the top,

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.210
you'll receive bonus points you
can add to your next written exam.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.490
It can be very helpful for your tests.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:57.930
For real?!

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.490
Heck yeah!

00:05:59.100 --> 00:05:59.920
Wait, what?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:00.490
Really?

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:01.680
That's amazing!

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.920
<i>If it sounds too good to
be true, it usually is.</i>

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:02.170
Crazy!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.920
Could we use it to prevent failing?

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.670
lowest ten placers receive a penalty

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.530
A truly desirous result!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:07.670
<i>The lowest ten placers receive a penalty.</i>

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.930
Come on, guys, keep it down!

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:12.680
Ma'am, what's this...

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.640
What's this penalty?

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:22.450
The bottom ten first-year placers will lose
ten points on their next written exam.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.400
Say what?!

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.280
So we can lose points on our exams, too?!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.910
I knew it!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.080
That's so bad...

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.540
Might be hard not to fail...

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.280
What? What?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.340
Seems pretty bad.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:40.040
The materials I handed out also provide
a list of each sports festival event.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.990
Yeah, pretty bad...

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.660
I had a feeling it might be so...

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.040
Keep it down, guys!

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:45.550
Event List
Mandatory Events
1. 100 Meter Dash
2. Hurdles
3. Topple the Pole (Boys Only)
4. Ball Toss (Girls Only)
5. Tug-of-War (Gender Segregated)
6. Obstacle Course
7. Three-Legged Race
8. Piggyback Joust
9. 200 Meter Dash
Voluntary Events
10. Scavenger Hunt
11. Four-Way Tug-of-War
12. Co-Ed Three-Legged Race
13. Combined Class Year 1200 Meter Relay

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.990
<i>Thirteen events in all.</i>

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.920
This is pretty hardcore...

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.550
We can't cover all this in one day!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:51.800
We can.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.320
There's no cheerleading or
dance competition, after all.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:07:00.150
It will be purely a test
of stamina and athleticism.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:04.060
Decide for yourselves who will
participate and in what order.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.690
Fill in the participant
sheet and submit it to me.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.570
How much are we allowed to decide on our own?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.200
Everything.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:18.580
You can decide everything about the
events, including who's in which heat.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:36.640
The island and cruise ship tests
had infinite possibilities.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.450
I've realized that's the case now.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.600
So this time, as wellвЂ”

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.280
What do you think

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.950
makes this test significantly different
from the previous special tests?

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.600
It seems like another special test to me.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:57.400
The structure and effect on points seems
identical to previous special tests.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:58.600
That is true.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.620
On paper, it's the same.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.870
But in practice, it's different.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.130
For instance, the written exam.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.390
Although there was the hidden trick
regarding buying things with points,

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.060
fundamentally, it was still
a test of academic ability.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.510
You think the sports
festival is the same way?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.800
We should assume that stamina and athletic
ability are the order of the day.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:22.930
Sneaky tricks won't have much
bearing on the results.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:29.630
The most important thing here is
strict preparation before the event.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.090
That's all.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:35.030
Preparation is just what I'm talking about.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.910
You're looking for quick fixes, loopholes.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.580
Like having someone be absent
before the competition,

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.540
or forcing them drop out partway.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:45.540
I wasn't

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.790
In other words, you want a surefire method.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:55.180
Are you suggesting we have to fight
and win through orthodox means?

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.820
It's up to you how you take it.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.430
C'mon, we gotta do it based on skill!

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.690
I know myself best of all.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.210
If I win, the class wins!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.320
That's best for everyone!

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:14.690
You think so?

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:16.820
Probability-wise, maybe...

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:21.330
If you want to take on all the
voluntary events, I'm okay with that.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.920
Then it's settled!

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:26.790
I'll take part in all the voluntary events!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.680
If everyone agrees with the skill method,
then the voluntary eventsвЂ”

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:33.050
How to decide on voluntary event participation?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:33.050
Skill Method
Give priority placements to the skilled
Positive: Gives a high chance of winning
Negative: Gives others (less strong) little chance of winning;
ignores the will of other classmates

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:33.050
Voluntary Method
Choose placements based on what each person wants
Positive: Gives people the order they want; lets everyone enjoy themselves
Negative: Not everyone will get what they want; potential inconsistency of results

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.440
Wait.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.250
I have a supplementary proposal.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:40.090
Between the two options, I have
no objection to the skill method.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:45.000
But there's no guarantee that we can beat
the other classes through that alone.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.310
That's true.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.410
While it's a given that we should put

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:53.070
our most athletic members in the
voluntary events where they specialize,

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.100
we can also best bring out

00:09:55.100 --> 00:10:00.570
our maximum potential in the mandatory
events through optimized combinations.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:01.480
For instance,

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:04.570
rather than putting two fast people
in a race together, eliminating one,

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:07.670
we should pair each with a slow person
to guarantee higher placements.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.210
Wait a minute.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:14.500
Doesn't that plan reduce the chances of
non-athletic people winning anything?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.550
And we'll lose our chances
of getting the bonus...

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.300
What a disappointment 'twould be!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:25.640
I understand the desire to
not lose private points, too.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.870
An ultimate class victory will benefit
the individuals in the long run.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.270
Why is this an issue?

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:34.690
B-But high placements get us
big bonuses on our next exam!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.780
Besides, isn't quitting unfair?

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.280
I understand why you feel that way.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.410
In that caseвЂ”

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.440
But your priorities are misplaced.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.820
Just focus on your studies to the point
where you don't have to rely on bonuses.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.870
The bonuses are only given to
the top three placers, anyway,

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.950
so it's not that much of a problem, is it?

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:58.540
Is there an event you believe you
can place third or higher in?

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.090
Well...

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.720
May I?

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.230
Horikita-san's suggestion...

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.180
Sorry, but it doesn't work for me.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:26.990
2nd Season

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:26.990
Classroom
of
the
Elite

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:34.130
That's a very vague objection.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:37.380
Well, I'm not as smart as you, Horikita-san.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.510
I thought it was an entirely
reasonable proposal.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:45.890
I just don't get it!

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.890
What exactly don't you "get"?

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.250
All of it?

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:53.060
Why don't you explain it so
even an idiot can understand?

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:57.930
Oh, right. You don't deal with idiots.

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:59.660
I didn't say that.

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.070
Did so!

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:06.450
Like Shinohara-san said, how can you
want to see the other students fail?

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.210
They'll be rewarded in the long run.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:11.450
And you blamed people too stupid
to pass a test on their own?

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:15.210
How do you expect our class
to unite with that attitude?

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:17.840
That was the point of my suggestion.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.840
Well, that's Horikita-san's idea.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.720
What do you think, Kushida-san?

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.550
Huh? Me?!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:26.470
Yeah.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.030
It's tricky, isn't it?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.480
I feel like I understand both sides!

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.790
Ideally, I think you'd combine both ideas.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:43.010
So that the people taking first
and last both feel okay about it.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:43.980
True.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.240
That'd be for the best.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.490
I've thought of that, of course.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.990
A way for both sides to be satisfied.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:56.220
Have students who don't need
test points take the top places,

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:58.580
then average out the private points
they gain with the ones the students

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.000
in the bottom ranks lose.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:03.260
We'll share gains and losses among the class.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.260
Hey, great idea!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:08.450
But that's just for the points.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.570
It also lowers our chances of winning.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.270
What do you guys think?

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.390
If Karuizawa-san's against it, I am, too.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.570
So am I.

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:19.400
Yeah! I agree with Karuizawa-san!

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.110
Are you people stupid?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.480
You're against it because she is?

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.110
That's not logical!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:30.980
The other classes can't possibly
have members as stupid as you all.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:32.870
How do you know?

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.590
Point is, I'm against it.

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:37.850
And plenty of others are
clearly against it, too.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.960
Horikita-san, you're just cruel.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.090
She is.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:44.680
Yeah.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:47.470
I thought you were nicer than this...

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.340
Calm down, both of you.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.700
If we can't agree,

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:54.410
we can settle this with a vote.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.120
If Yosuke-kun says it, I'm in!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:01.980
Horikita-san's idea is to
focus entirely on skill,

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:06.490
while Karuizawa-san's is to allow
personal opinion into discussion.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.860
Let's have a show of hands.

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:12.130
First, who agrees with Horikita-san's idea?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.000
Looks like ten votes.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.530
Hey, Ayanokoji-kun!

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:22.000
Don't worry. I'm abstaining.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.520
Next, Karuizawa-san's combined plan.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.250
Who agrees with that?

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:33.010
Thank you.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.520
The result of the vote is...

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.390
Ten votes for Horikita-san's idea.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:39.020
Eight votes for Karuizawa-san's idea.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.010
The rest abstained, I guess.

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:42.270
Heck yeah!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.400
Now, regarding participation for each event,

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.800
let's take some dedicated time to discuss it.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.900
Okay!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.280
I'm in for all the events!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.310
Sudo-dono is so quick to act!

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:57.410
Just leave it all to me!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.650
Isn't this one cute?

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.170
Yeah, totally cute!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.560
Right?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.820
Excuse me!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.380
That email you sent me.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.800
Mind telling me what it was all about?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.300
The bonuses are only given to
the top three placers, anyway,

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.390
so it's not that much of a problem, is it?

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:13.970
<b>Cancel</b>

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.450
<b>You Have a New Message</b>

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.450
<b>Sender: A</b>

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.450
<b>Open</b>

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.810
Is there an event you believe you
can place third or higher in?

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:18.810
From: A
To: Karuizawa Kei
Subject: None
Find a way to oppose Horikita's suggestion.
When you do, ask for Kushida's opinion, too.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:20.780
Well...

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:24.080
You cooked up a good argument on the spot.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:29.320
I actually agreed with
Horikita-san's opinion, though...

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.820
And I don't understand why you wanted
me to get Kushida-san's opinion.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.240
What was the point of the order?

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:38.620
If you need to understand the
reasoning behind everything I do,

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.120
we'll never get anywhere.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:42.830
Besides, I won't always tell you.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.340
Then tell me one other thing.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.580
What is it you want?

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.830
To bring Class D to Class A.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.960
I'm sure Horikita believes that.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.650
That's not what I mean!

00:15:57.650 --> 00:16:00.100
I want to know what <i>you're</i> after.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.450
Oh, that?

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:06.520
I'm happy to make my current class
one capable of rising to Class A.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.480
That's how I've begun to feel.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:09.970
What in the world?

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.110
You think you're that much better than us?

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:15.230
You wouldn't believe me if I told you now.

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:17.130
And I can't prove it to you.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:21.750
So I'm going to create a framework
to allow you to believe me.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:26.060
During this sports festival, Class D...

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.630
will produce a traitor.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:35.510
The traitor will likely spill all of
Class D's internal information to others.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.010
Wait

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:38.060
What?!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.050
G-Give me something more concrete than that!

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.390
I will, when the time comes.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.530
A t-traitor?

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:48.520
Isn't that dangerous?

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.080
The groundwork has been laid.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.780
Now, go. We'll attract
too much attention here.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.040
<b>Event Player Selection</b>

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:02.610
Be amazed!

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.540
<b>Aptitude Tests</b>

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:04.320
That's amazing!

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.040
Awesome!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.370
How's that?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.350
11.5, looks like!

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:17.250
I pulled 82.4!

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:19.820
How dang strong are you?!

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.290
Over 80!

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.970
I've been workin' out.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:24.310
Obviously.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.960
You do it, too, Koenji.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.940
I'd prefer not.

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.190
Here, Ayanokoji.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.220
Yeah! Hope I get a good result!

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:36.820
What's wrong?

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.320
Show me your grip strength, Ike-dono!

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.320
What's the boys' average grip strength?

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.000
About 60, maybe?

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.450
Sixty?

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:48.660
<i>Grip strength isn't necessarily proportional
to the thickness of one's arms.</i>

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.880
<i>What matters is the muscles
in the forearm called</i>

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.170
<i>the brachioradialis and
flexor carpi radialis.</i>

00:17:56.560 --> 00:18:00.420
<i>Working these out will
increase grip strength.</i>

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.280
<i>In other words,</i>

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.910
<i>as long as you have
sufficient muscle mass,</i>

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:08.600
<i>you can train it to surpass 100 kilograms.</i>

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.790
<i>That should be acceptable.</i>

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:13.770
It won't go any further.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.040
What's your score?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:17.910
60.6.

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.010
Wow.

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.490
You're strong, Ayanokoji-kun.

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.700
No, I think that's about average...

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.370
The average would be lower than that.

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.440
It's around 45, or maybe 50.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.380
Take that!

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.630
It's a 42.6.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.360
Couldn't you nudge me up to a 50?!

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:38.200
Ike-kun scores 42.6.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:42.030
<i>Oh, so 60 is on the higher side.</i>

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.330
All done!

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.330
Let's see. I got...

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:49.710
Heck yeah!

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:52.150
I'm in for all the voluntary events!

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:54.960
The information we just
agreed on is very important,

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.370
Just watch, you guys!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.050
How excited he is!

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.900
so write down only your own roles.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.770
Sure, okay.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:02.910
Don't take pictures or
leave any other record.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:10.010
You gotta go harder than that!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.490
Keep your hips low!

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:14.290
L-Like this?!

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.690
Really put your back into it!

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.490
I'm your leader, so you gotta keep up!

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.300
We're winnin' this, guys!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.570
Y-Yeah...

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:22.300
I can't hear you!

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.530
Horikita-san, you're running too fast.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.690
It's true that our rhythm is off,

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.330
but only because you're too slow.

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.810
Shouldn't the slower person try
to match the rhythm of the faster?

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:37.850
Who wants to compromise to
make their own times slower?

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.370
Can we talk?

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:48.700
About what?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:53.540
I think you need to learn
to compromise a little more.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:57.420
I'm only being stubborn because I want
to get us the best possible time.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:59.060
In the three-legged race,

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:03.340
it's logical that the relatively slower
people should be made to pace up.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:05.650
You're inflexible on this point?

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:06.370
Yes.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:11.540
That will lower the number of people
willing to practice with you.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:16.940
I can't match my rhythm to those
who refuse to work from the start.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.320
Give me your leg.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.890
Why?

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:24.870
Run a race with me.

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:27.080
Why should I?

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.410
There's a co-ed three-legged race.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:33.010
We should try to assess our suitability
as partners, shouldn't we?

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.530
You think you can keep up with me?

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.150
You'll just slow me down.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:42.470
Logically speaking,
speed shouldn't matter, should it?

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:44.720
Very well.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.120
I'll tie us together.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.560
Let's begin.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.880
H-Hey!

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.450
It shouldn't be hard to match my rhythm.

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:02.030
I know that!

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:19.050
It's not about individual speed.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.840
The problem is that you
won't look at your partner.

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:29.350
Looking at your partner and giving them a
degree of initiative is what's important.

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:33.670
Horikita.

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:35.590
Come out with me a while tomorrow.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.230
What?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:41.230
You, I, and one other,

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.560
will embark on Team White reconnaissance.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:45.490
Yeah, that might work!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.490
One other?

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:47.330
Kushida.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:49.950
Why?

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:53.990
The Earth Group traitor
during the cruise exam...

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.500
You're so reliable!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:56.500
was her.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.530
I appreciate you helping
everyone, too, Kushida-san.

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:01.520
Oh, don't say that!
